{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:2d8c2cd4ce22f6ce","name":"Prowler-Class Reconnaissance Vessel","source":{"id":"source:reference-2d8c2cd4ce22f6ce","title":"Prowler-Class Reconnaissance Vessel","revision":21231,"timestamp":"2024-08-26T01:24:06Z","sha256":"9d2eed36e11f649eadfed172532361d267579d6502d86d0f411082f1f59eacff","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=21231","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Prowler-Class%20Reconnaissance%20Vessel&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-2d8c2cd4ce22f6ce","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Galaxy of Intrigue"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Galaxy_of_Intrigue"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Affiliations: ",{"tag":"a","children":["The New Republic"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_New_Republic","referenceId":"reference:e6046dbb57e5abb0"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["For longer reconnaissance and spy missions, ",{"tag":"a","children":["The New Republic"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_New_Republic","referenceId":"reference:e6046dbb57e5abb0"}," depends on its top-secret ",{"tag":"i","children":["Prowler"]},"-Class Reconnaissance Vessel. The ",{"tag":"i","children":["Prowler"]},"-Class is basically an expanded ",{"tag":"a","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Ferret"]},"-Class Reconnaissance Vessel"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Ferret-Class_Reconnaissance_Vessel","referenceId":"reference:8f1666405dbd689d"}," containing less equipment. The ship is intended for two-to three-month tours while its crew works to keep it from becoming a target. Like the ",{"tag":"i","children":["Ferret"]},"-Class, the ",{"tag":"i","children":["Prowler"]}," operates on ion engines, is coated with sensor-evading materials, and features an advanced masking system.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["A ",{"tag":"i","children":["Prowler"]}," is designed for stealth and, therefore, gains a +4 Technology bonus to ",{"tag":"a","children":["Stealth"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Stealth","referenceId":"reference:526a40a447ddd7aa"}," checks to hide the ship. When its sublight baffled drive is active, the ship moves at half its normal ",{"tag":"a","children":["Speed"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Speed","referenceId":"reference:c372fee9b4566b85"}," but gains an additional +4 Technology bonus to ",{"tag":"a","children":["Stealth"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Stealth","referenceId":"reference:526a40a447ddd7aa"}," checks to avoid detection. The ",{"tag":"i","children":["Prowler"]},"-Class can run on its baffled drive for only three hours.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The ship has a complement of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Sensor Decoys"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Sensor_Decoys?action=edit&redlink=1"}," that can be deployed in the event of discovery. If the decoys are deployed, the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicle Pilot"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicle_Pilot","referenceId":"reference:4aff6d0e54fff36e"}," can reroll a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Stealth"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Stealth","referenceId":"reference:526a40a447ddd7aa"}," check once per encounter. The ",{"tag":"i","children":["Prowler"]},"-Class Reconnaissance Vessel contains enough ",{"tag":"a","children":["Sensor Decoys"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Sensor_Decoys?action=edit&redlink=1"}," to use this capability four times before needing to resupply.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Default (Expert)"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Prowler"]},"-Class Reconnaissance Vessel Statistics (CL 12)"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Gargantuan ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starfighter"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starfighter"},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Initiative"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Initiative","referenceId":"referenc